<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy · Intervene"
  description="Privacy policy for the Intervene Limited website."
  heading="Privacy policy."
  updated="July 2026 (v3)"
  current="legal"
>
  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Intervene Limited is an independent advisory practice based in the
    United Kingdom, registered in England and Wales under company number
    17317647, with registered office at 71-75 Shelton Street, London
    WC2H 9JQ. For the purposes of UK GDPR, Intervene Limited is the
    data controller for any personal data submitted via this site or in the
    course of a confidential enquiry.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
  <p>Through the contact form, we collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Name</li>
    <li>Organisation</li>
    <li>Email address</li>
    <li>Role (optional)</li>
    <li>The free-text description of the situation prompting the enquiry</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    With your consent, this site uses Google Analytics (GA4) to understand
    how pages are used. Analytics runs only after you accept via the cookie
    notice. Until then, and if you decline, no analytics cookies are set and
    no analytics data is collected. When enabled, Google Analytics records
    usage data such as pages viewed, approximate location derived from a
    truncated IP address, and device and browser type. We use no advertising
    trackers and do not profile visitors for marketing. Beyond Google
    Analytics and the Google Fonts CDN, which serves typeface files, this
    site uses no third-party scripts. You can change your choice at any time
    via "Cookies" in the footer.
  </p>
  <p>
    Two things are stored in your own browser regardless of that choice,
    because the site cannot do what you have asked without them. Your accept
    or decline is stored so the notice does not ask again on every page, and
    if you use the Snapshot your answers are held in the tab so the result
    survives a refresh. Neither is used to track you, neither is sent
    anywhere, and closing the tab discards the Snapshot answers.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How we use it</h2>
  <p>
    Personal data is used solely to respond to the enquiry and to determine
    whether an engagement is appropriate. It is not used for marketing, not
    shared with third parties, and not retained beyond what is necessary to
    handle the enquiry or to comply with the engagement-related
    record-keeping obligations of an active or recently concluded contract.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Third-party processors</h2>
  <p>
    The contact form and the Snapshot follow-up form are transmitted via
    Formspree (Formspree, Inc.), which acts solely as the transmission
    mechanism. Formspree is established in the United States, so submitting
    either form transfers what you entered to the United States. Formspree's
    processing is governed by its own data processing terms. No other
    third-party processor receives form submissions.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site itself is static and is hosted on GitHub Pages (GitHub, Inc.).
    Serving a page involves GitHub receiving your request, including your IP
    address, in the ordinary course of delivering the site. We do not have
    access to those server logs and we do not use them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where you consent to analytics, Google Analytics is provided by Google
    Ireland Limited (with Google LLC in the United States) and processes
    site-usage data on our behalf under Google's data processing terms.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Intervention Readiness Snapshot</h2>
  <p>
    The Intervention Readiness Snapshot asks ten multiple-choice questions
    about a single system. It is a self-reported instrument. It does not
    assess your organisation, and it does not test anything you enter against
    evidence.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Completing the Snapshot.</strong> Your answers are held in your
    own browser tab while you work and are used to display your result. No
    name, email address, organisation, role, sector or company size is
    requested, and there is no free-text field anywhere in the questionnaire.
    Nothing is sent to us unless you choose one of the two actions below.
    Closing the tab discards your answers.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>If you ask us to contact you or to send you your Snapshot.</strong>
    We collect your name and work email address, and your organisation and
    role if you choose to give them. We also receive a short summary of your
    own result, so that a reply can be about something specific. We use this
    to send what you asked for and to reply. We do not add you to a mailing
    list, because we do not operate one.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>If you contribute to the Intervention Readiness Index.</strong>
    That is a separate, optional action with its own control. It sends your
    ten answers and nothing else: no name, no email address, no organisation
    and no role. We use these to understand how organisations answer these
    questions and, in time, to publish aggregate findings. We will not publish
    any figure drawn from a group small enough to identify a respondent.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What we cannot yet claim.</strong> Both actions above are relayed
    by Formspree to a single mailbox. An Index contribution therefore arrives
    alongside contact enquiries, and although it carries no identifying field,
    we could in principle correlate two messages sent close together in time.
    We are honest about this rather than describing the contribution as
    anonymous. A future version will separate the two paths properly, and this
    notice will be updated when it does.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Retention.</strong> Snapshot enquiries are handled as ordinary
    enquiries and deleted twelve months from the close of correspondence,
    unless an active engagement requires otherwise. Index contributions carry no identifier and are
    retained for trend analysis.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Lawful basis.</strong> Where you ask us to contact you or send you
    something, we rely on Article 6(1)(b), taking steps at your request, and
    Article 6(1)(f), our legitimate interest in responding to enquiries. Index
    contribution relies on your consent, given by ticking the box on that
    control. You can complete the Snapshot and read your result without doing
    either.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under UK GDPR you have the right to access, correct, or request deletion
    of personal data we hold about you. To exercise these rights, use the
    <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. We respond to such requests within
    one calendar month.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    This policy is governed by UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018. The
    supervisory authority for England and Wales is the Information
    Commissioner's Office
    (<a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>).
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
